    <!-- =========================================================
         1. DEFINITION OF CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION
    ========================================================== -->

    <div class="undertaking-main-section">

        <div class="undertaking-main-title">
            1. Definition of Confidential Information
        </div>


        <div class="undertaking-paragraph">

            “<strong>Confidential Information</strong>” means any and all
            information, data, or material (whether oral, written, electronic,
            or in any other form) disclosed or made available by the Company
            or its clients to the Employee, or which the Employee learns,
            develops, or has access to during the course of employment.

        </div>


        <div class="undertaking-paragraph">

            This includes, without limitation:

        </div>


        <ul class="undertaking-list">

            <li>
                Client lists, customer data, call recordings, scripts,
                transaction details, personal data of customers, and any
                information protected under the Information Technology Act,
                2000 (including rules on sensitive personal data).
            </li>

            <li>
                Business processes, Staundertakingrd Operating Procedures (SOPs),
                training materials, workflows, software tools, databases,
                and proprietary methodologies.
            </li>

            <li>
                Trade secrets, know-how, technical data, financial
                information, marketing strategies, pricing models, vendor
                details, and intellectual property.
            </li>

            <li>
                Any information marked “confidential” or which a reasonable
                person would understand to be confidential in the BPO context.
            </li>

            <li>
                Information relating to the Company’s or its clients’
                business plans, strategies, or operations.
            </li>

        </ul>


        <!-- =====================================================
             EXCLUSIONS
        ====================================================== -->

        <div class="undertaking-paragraph undertaking-sub-heading">

            Confidential Information shall not include information that:

        </div>


        <ul class="undertaking-list undertaking-exclusion-list">

            <li>
                Is or becomes publicly available through no fault of the
                Employee.
            </li>

            <li>
                Was lawfully known to the Employee prior to disclosure by
                the Company (with documentary proof).
            </li>

            <li>
                Is independently developed by the Employee without use of
                or reference to the Company’s Confidential Information.
            </li>

            <li>
                Is required to be disclosed by law (provided the Employee
                gives prompt written notice to the Company to seek protective
                measures).
            </li>

        </ul>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================================================
         2. OBLIGATIONS OF THE EMPLOYEE
